  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A is linked to JM1 through a series of molecular interactions, with the final pathway highlighting a direct target relationship. The drug targets 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is then targeted by (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol, a compound that itself is targeted by Miyabenol A. This suggests a chain of molecular interactions where Miyabenol A influences the activity of a proteasome subunit, which in turn affects the function of the compound that ultimately targets JM1. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Miyabenol A and JM1 through a series of target interactions, with the proteasome subunit acting as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
